ojsdn patches for wmediumd, as one diff against https://github.com/ramonfontes/wmediumd commit
63e9fc995cfb260065c7a0d4c2b14f715f224436 (branch mininet-wifi). Same result as install/wmediumd_ojsdn.py,
which the image build and install/patch-wmediumd.sh apply to that commit. Every change is opt-in
through an environment variable that common/topo.py sets from the run configuration; with none set, wmediumd
behaves as the original:
  OJSDN_WMD_RCVBUF        receive buffer of the hwsim netlink socket (medium_rcvbuf_kb)
  OJSDN_WMD_PER_CHANNEL   contention per channel instead of one medium for all radios (medium_per_channel)
  OJSDN_WMD_MAXQ_US       bounded queue: a frame that would wait longer is dropped as a failed transmission
                          (medium_max_queue_ms)
  OJSDN_WMD_STATS         per-second counters of queued and dropped frames
Apply in a wmediumd checkout:  patch -p1 < wmediumd-ojsdn.patch
License: GPL-2.0-or-later, as wmediumd.
